    Bug 2001556 - Fix issues in browser.tabs.move(). r=aleca


    This patch brings `tabs.move()` closer to Mozilla’s implementation, particularly
    regarding index calculation logic. It also fixes an implementation error where
    moving a tab from left to right would not place the tab at the correct index [1].
    The correct behavior is now covered by tests.

    The primary mail tab in a normal Thunderbird window is not movable. However, the
    API previously allowed moving this tab, which caused various issues because the
    UI assumes that the first tab is always the primary mail tab. This patch enforces
    that constraint.

    The main error reported in the bug was caused by assuming that all tabs have an
    active browser, which is not always the case.

    During work on tabs.move(), it was also discovered that tabs moved to another
    window are assigned a new tab ID. This deviates from Mozilla’s behavior and was
    never tested. A follow-up patch will address this.

    [1]: Wrong test: Move to index 3, but test at index 2 (https://searchfox.org/comm-central/rev/c64a585f6727f405cb1eb9174193fb7e8b4dadf5/mail/components/extensions/test/browser/browser_ext_tabs_move.js#147,163)

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D274059

